#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-transformation.md
msgid "CAP-TRANSFORMATION.1"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-transformation.md
msgid "MUST"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-transformation.md
msgid "Models are versioned SQL (or equivalent) in bronze, silver and gold tiers, with tests that run in CI."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-transformation.md
msgid "CI builds and tests the models on every change."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-transformation.md
msgid "CAP-TRANSFORMATION.2"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-transformation.md
msgid "Conformance happens once, in silver: each entity has one identifier shared by every consumer."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-transformation.md
msgid "Gold models join on silver identifiers only."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-transformation.md
msgid "CAP-TRANSFORMATION.3"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-transformation.md
msgid "No measure or report value is computed in an application; applications select and format gold."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-transformation.md
msgid "A test forbids the application's reporting code from opening a database connection to operational tables."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-transformation.md
msgid "CAP-TRANSFORMATION.4"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-transformation.md
msgid "Development runs write to development schemas inside the production catalog, which no consumer is granted."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-transformation.md
msgid "Development schemas carry no consumer grants."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-transformation.md
msgid "CAP-TRANSFORMATION.5"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-transformation.md
msgid "SHOULD"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-transformation.md
msgid "Gold stores counts and sums, not ratios, so measures re-aggregate correctly.{1}*Example:* Gold stores 'enrolled 412' and 'population 455', not '90.5 per cent', so a district figure is the sum of counts divided once, not an average of school percentages."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-transformation.md
msgid "Review gold columns; ratios are computed in the semantic layer."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-transformation.md
msgid "CAP-TRANSFORMATION.6"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-transformation.md
msgid "Silver keeps effective-dated history for every relationship that changes over time (enrolment, posting, guardianship, programme), with valid-from, valid-to and recorded-at, and gold is computed as at a declared reference date.{1}*Example:* An enrolment valid from 2025-09-01 to 2026-03-15 is counted by a census with reference date 2026-02-01 and not by one dated 2026-10-01."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-transformation.md
msgid "Silver relationship tables carry the three time columns; each gold model names its reference-date rule."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-transformation.md
msgid "CAP-TRANSFORMATION.7"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-transformation.md
msgid "A document about one record, such as a certificate, transcript or letter, may be produced by an application from operational data; any aggregate it prints (a rank, an average) comes from gold or the semantic layer.{1}*Example:* A transcript lists one learner's results straight from operational data, but the class average printed on it comes from the semantic layer."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-transformation.md
msgid "Document templates read aggregates only through the semantic layer or gold."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-transformation.md
msgid "CAP-TRANSFORMATION.8"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-transformation.md
msgid "Credentials issued about a single record, such as certificates and transcripts, are W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0, using Open Badges 3.0 or CLR 2.0 where they fit."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-transformation.md
msgid "An issued credential fixture verifies with a standard verifier."
msgstr ""

